Subject: [PATCH] WIP: dead-card AI fixes for Azorius Momo and Dimir Uldaros
 (paused)

Paused at the coordinator's request; nothing is measured yet. The one
draft lives in mtgsim/forge_patches/pending/, which setup --build does not
read (load_patches only globs the top-level folder), so no engine changes.
Scope: Practiced Offense, Springleaf Drum, Nurturing Pixie (Azorius Momo);
Uldaros Theorix, Seasoned Cryomancer (Dimir Uldaros). Not to be touched:
patches 0001/0002 (coordinator's Azorius Control work), Countersculpt,
Theorist's Sanctum, Vraska's Final Mercy. My patches start at 0003.

Baseline (runs/baseline-rr-n30-s1/games.jsonl, 30 games per pairing, seed
1; seen = in opening hand or drawn, cast = players[].played > 0), which I
reproduced exactly:
  azorius-momo (300 games): Practiced Offense seen 184 cast 0; Springleaf
    Drum seen 230 cast 0; Nurturing Pixie seen 165 cast 5. For comparison,
    Momo 227/210, Starfield Shepherd 219/203, Sage of the Skies 227/206.
  dimir-uldaros (300 games): Uldaros Theorix seen 188 cast 3; Seasoned
    Cryomancer seen 209 cast 7 (Deceit 232/218, Overlord 141/130).
  Median own turns in those games: 8-10, so mana value is not the blocker.

Findings so far (shared ~/.mtgsim/forge, read only; line numbers at
FORGE_PINNED_REF 7db198d72e):

1. Springleaf Drum - CAUSE FOUND. AiController.java ~2025-2031:
   saList.removeIf(... ComputerUtilCard.isCardRemAIDeck(h) && !flatMc ...)
   drops every AI:RemoveDeck:All card from the candidate plays unless Flat
   Monte Carlo is on. With --mc off (the default) the Drum is never
   considered. Only Flat MC offers it (isRemoveDeckManaPermanent, ~2637).
   DRAFT: pending/0003-springleaf-drum-ai-playable.patch removes the
   AI:RemoveDeck:All line. Still to check before measuring: can
   ComputerUtilMana pay its mana ability "T tapXType<1/Creature>" (grep
   ComputerUtilMana for CostTapType / tapXType)? Does tapping a creature
   for mana cost the AI attacks? Also look at ComputerUtilAbility.java
   ~339, another isCardRemAIDeck check. If the AI casts the Drum but never
   taps it, the patch is a net loss: measure and drop it if so.

2. Nurturing Pixie - HYPOTHESIS from reading the code, not yet confirmed
   in game logs. For a creature spell, AiController.saSideEffects ->
   checkETBEffects (~293-450) runs each mandatory ETB trigger through
   doTrigger(exSA, false). If the AI would not use the trigger, the
   creature is rejected (BadEtbEffects). The exemption at ~436 (AILogic$
   BadETB) applies only when the trigger is NOT fully targetable, so it
   does not help while the AI controls a nonland permanent. The trigger
   (ChangeZone Battlefield->Hand, ValidTgts Permanent.nonFaerie+nonLand+
   YouCtrl, TargetMin 0) goes to ChangeZoneAi.knownOriginTriggerAI
   (~1458) -> isPreferredTarget (~865). For Battlefield origin, ~1094
   filters to opponents' cards unless the ability has AITgtOwnCards, so
   with only own targets the list is empty. canBouncePermanent (saving a
   threatened permanent) is the only path to yes. Next: read
   isUnpreferredTarget (~1369) with mandatory=false; confirm with
   --save-logs games; compare Mischievous Pup (same "up to one other
   target permanent you control" shape, no hint). Candidate fixes to
   evaluate: OptionalDecider$ You on the trigger (equivalent in rules,
   since choosing zero targets does nothing, but check the +1/+1 counter
   condition still works), or AITgtOwnCards plus a sensible target such
   as a permanent with an ETB.

3. Practiced Offense - NOT YET INVESTIGATED. Script: SP$ PutCounterAll |
   ValidTgts$ Player | ValidCards$ Creature (P1P1) with SubAbility DB$ Pump
   | ValidTgts$ Creature | KWChoice$ Double Strike,Lifelink; Flashback 1W.
   Next: read ability/PutCounterAllAi.java (does it handle a targeted
   player and target itself?) and PumpAi's handling of KWChoice as a
   sub-ability.

4. Uldaros Theorix - HYPOTHESIS. Same checkETBEffects path: the ETB
   (ValidCard Card.Self+wasCastByYou, no OptionalDecider) starts a chain of
   DB$ Pump with TgtZone Graveyard, TargetMin 0, and no NumAtt/KW, then
   ChangeZone exile and Play WithoutManaCost CopyCard WithTotalCMC 6.
   PumpAi probably refuses a pump with no effect aimed at graveyard cards
   -> BadEtbEffects -> the 6-drop is never cast. Next: read PumpAi
   (pumpTgtAI / TgtZone handling) and confirm with --save-logs. Candidate
   fix: an AILogic on the Pump chain that PumpAi accepts (look for one
   meaning "always" or "pick from graveyard"), or OptionalDecider on the
   trigger. Also check that the Play step then actually casts the copies.

5. Seasoned Cryomancer - HYPOTHESIS. ETB DB$ Draw 2 -> DB$ Discard 2
   (Mode TgtChoose, no Defined) -> ImmediateTrigger tap+stun. DrawAi
   (sub-ability check) or DiscardAi (discarding from own hand) likely
   refuses -> BadEtbEffects. Next: read DrawAi (trigger / sub-ability
   handling) and DiscardAi (Mode TgtChoose with no target -> defaults to
   the activator?); compare other loot-on-ETB creatures' scripts.

Next steps, in order:
 a. Finish the code reading above; confirm each cause with a few games
    with --save-logs (any engine run goes through the lock below).
 b. Write one patch per concern as mtgsim/forge_patches/pending/NNNN-*.patch
    (0003 onward), following mtgsim/forge_patches/README.md. Move a patch
    to mtgsim/forge_patches/ only once it is measured.
 c. Measure on a private copy, never the shared checkout:
      export MTGSIM_HOME=<scratch>/dead-cards-home
      cp -a ~/.mtgsim/forge $MTGSIM_HOME/forge
      echo '{"forge_dir": "'$MTGSIM_HOME/forge'"}' > $MTGSIM_HOME/config.json
    Every engine command goes through
      flock /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-Mtg-simulator/ac175026-a9a0-5278-9b10-d7c0563130a0/scratchpad/engine.lock ...
    in the background (the queue is shared). Per deck: gauntlet
    decks/standard/meta/<deck>.txt --vs <the other ten meta .txt> -n 100
    --seed 1, once without and once with that deck's patches (setup --build
    in between, with the patch copied into the top-level folder of a
    scratch copy of the repo or of this worktree). Report the win rate with
    its 95% interval, before and after, and how often the fixed card is now
    cast. Then a mirror on the patched engine: match <deck> <deck> -n 200
    --seed 1, which should come out near 50%. Put the numbers in each
    patch's Measured: line.
 d. Commit on this branch, delete the private Forge copy, report back.

